   "html_text": "To see how these views diverge, consider the following case which is similar to a case described by Ross (2012: 87–88): at ⟦M⟧ Sally has the ability to immediately form an intention to ⟨not kill anyone five years later at ⟦M⟧ ⟩, although ⟨killing no one at ⟦M⟧ ⟩ is not scrupulously securable for Sally at ⟦M⟧ . On the other hand, killing exactly one person or killing exactly two persons at ⟦M⟧ are both scrupulously securable for Sally at ⟦M⟧ . According to Portmore’s securitism, one of the object",
